Subject: [PATCH] Re-pins: the mutual-dependence exception
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner ruling, 2026-11-07 (card, about 08:43Z, "A. Allow the exception"):
a re-pin may share a PR with a change only when the two are mutually
dependent, neither passing on its own, and the PR body says why. Example:
folio-assistant-core#639 (core re-pinned to cat-harness#1032 fails
check:tools without #639's library topic; #639 alone declares the library
topic twice against the old pin). A change that merely needs the new pins
still stacks.

In remote-mount §"Re-pinning", index-config, and merge-manager-watcher
sweep rule 10 (the merge manager checks the stated reason).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
